  22:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c ****  *
  23:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c ****  *  \details  \n
  24:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** <b>Functional Safety ROM CRC-16 Supervision Component - Top-Level Design </b>
  25:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  26:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  27:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \li<b>Package Model </b>\n
  28:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \image html Package_Rom.jpg
  29:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  30:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  31:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** The fsRom package provides the parts outlined in the model. In order to save space, there are diffe
ARM GAS  C:\Users\SX2605~1.HOD\AppData\Local\Temp\cc6jOYUR.s 			page 2


  32:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** depending what Rom modules exist and if some the modules are connected by means of I2C, or comparab
  33:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** By compilation switch, the Rom task handler may run either in the usual operating mode or in test h
  34:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** running in the usual operating mode, the test harness part will not be linked to the package. When 
  35:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** harness mode, separate data parts are provided, so the real Rom area is separated from being manipu
  36:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** test server will be able to change it.
  37:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  38:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  39:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** Test generation requires some ROM (flash memory) parts to be changed and restored again. This is  n
  40:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  41:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  42:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  43:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \li<b>State Model </b>\n
  44:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \image html StateModel_Rom.jpg
  45:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  46:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  47:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** Before checking the Rom, the Rom task handlers work area must be initialised correctly. This happen
  48:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** Rom task handler gets called and every time a full Rom check has been completed. After this initial
  49:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** handler transitions into the state "FSF_ROM_CHECK_ONGOING" and starts walking through the Rom space
  50:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** transitions back into state "FSF_ROM_CHECK_RESTART" and the process restarts again.
  51:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  52:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  53:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** None
  54:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  55:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  56:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  57:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \li<b>Scenario: Rom Supervision </b>\n
  58:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \image html SequenceChart_RomSupervision.jpg
  59:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  60:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** <b>Description </b>\n
  61:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** There is not that much to explain on this scenario.
  62:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** \n
  63:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** <b>Rationale </b>\n
  64:common/prog/FuncSafe/fsRom.c **** None
